{"change_summary":"Tightened denitrification acceptance coverage in `crates/tank_core/tests/denitrification.rs`: added a long-horizon planted-vs-unplanted fixture that initializes substrate zones from the engine model, strengthened the engine budget-ledger test to require a positive denitrification export metric matching the cumulative N2 export delta in a persistently suboxic setup, and extended the stoichiometry test to assert DIC production equals DOC consumption.","outstanding_risks":["Broader `tank_core` or workspace validation was not rerun; only the denitrification test target and formatting were executed in this pass."],"steps":[{"description":"Inspected the denitrification tests plus substrate-zone and budget-ledger code paths to determine how to preserve active denitrification under full engine execution.","order":0,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Patched `crates/tank_core/tests/denitrification.rs` to add a planted-vs-unplanted long-horizon fixture, require positive engine export attribution, and verify DIC stoichiometry.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Ran formatting and the denitrification test target to confirm the tightened assertions pass.","order":2,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo fmt --all` completed successfully.","`cargo test -p tank_core --test denitrification -- --nocapture` passed with 12/12 tests green.","The updated engine budget test now asserts a computed suboxic zone before and after the tick, a strictly positive `nitrogen_cycle.denitrification_n2_export_mg_n` metric, and equality between that metric and the cumulative N2 export delta.","The updated stoichiometry test now checks that denitrification increases dissolved inorganic carbon by the same mg C amount consumed from DOC within tolerance."]}